# =============================================================================
# .trivyignore — suppressed findings
# =============================================================================
# EMPTY ON PURPOSE. Nothing is currently suppressed.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# THE RULE FOR ADDING ANYTHING HERE
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# An ignore file is where security debt goes to be forgotten. Every entry must
# carry three things, or it does not go in:
#
#   1. WHY it is not exploitable HERE — not "it is only a HIGH", but a concrete
#      reason this code path is unreachable or the impact does not apply.
#   2. WHO decided, and when.
#   3. An EXPIRY date. Trivy enforces it: past that date the finding comes back
#      and breaks the build again, which forces a re-review instead of a
#      permanent silent exception.
#
# Format:
#   CVE-2024-12345 exp:2026-12-31
#
# Worked example of an acceptable entry:
#
#   # CVE-2025-0000 — glibc parser bug reachable only via setuid binaries.
#   # Our containers run as UID 1000/101 with capabilities: drop ALL and a
#   # read-only root filesystem, so there is no setuid path to reach it.
#   # No fixed version published upstream as of review.
#   # Reviewed: 2026-08-24. Re-check when Debian ships a patched glibc.
#   CVE-2025-0000 exp:2026-11-24
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WHAT DOES NOT BELONG HERE
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#   - "the build is red and I need to merge"        -> fix it or revert
#   - a CVE with an available fixed version         -> bump the dependency
#   - anything without an expiry date               -> that is not a decision,
#                                                      it is an abdication
#
# Note the pipeline already passes `--ignore-unfixed`, so findings with no
# upstream fix do not gate the build in the first place. If something reaches
# this file, a fix existed and was consciously deferred.
# =============================================================================
